  "enunciation": "If two triangles have two sides equal to two sides respectively, and have the angles contained by the equal straight lines equal, they will also have the base equal to the base, the triangle will be equal to the triangle, and the remaining angles will be equal.",
  "title_1080p": "I.4 \u2022 congruent triangles by SAS \u2022 Euclid's Elements",
  "title_short": "I.4 \u2022 congruent triangles by SAS \u2022 Euclid's Elements",
  "description": "\u201cIf two triangles have two sides equal to two sides respectively, and have the angles contained by the equal straight lines equal, they will also have the base equal to the base, the triangle will be equal to the triangle, and the remaining angles will be equal.\u201d\n\u2014 Euclid's Elements, BOOK I \u2022 PROP. 4 (G.24)\n\n00:00 1 \u00b7 GIVEN: triangles ABC and DEF with AB = DE\n00:09 2 \u00b7 GIVEN: AC = DF and angle BAC = EDF\n00:16 3 \u00b7 PROVE: BC = EF and \u25b3ABC = \u25b3DEF\n00:23 4 \u00b7 ASSERT: A \u2243 D and B \u2243 E\n00:35 5 \u00b7 ASSERT: AC \u2243 DF and C \u2243 F\n00:45 6 \u00b7 ASSERT: base BC \u2243 base EF\n00:53 7 \u00b7 ASSERT: BC = EF and \u25b3ABC = \u25b3DEF\n01:05 8 \u00b7 ASSERT: angle ABC = angle DEF\n01:14 9 \u00b7 \u2234: SAS congruence established\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 G.24 \u2022 v4",
